#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can now carry out the computation manually using `Sampler` and check the results on `Estimator`:\n"
msgstr "Agora podemos realizar o cálculo manualmente usando o `Sampler` e verificar os resultados com o `Estimator`:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical rigor (optional) {#mathematical-rigor-optional}"
msgstr "Rigor matemático (opcional) {#mathematical-rigor-optional}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expressing $|\\psi\\rangle$ with respect to the basis of eigenstates of $\\hat{H}$, $|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_\\lambda a_\\lambda |\\lambda\\rangle$, it follows:\n"
msgstr "Expressando $|\\psi\\rangle$ na base dos autoestados de $\\hat{H}$, $|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_\\lambda a_\\lambda |\\lambda\\rangle$, segue-se:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\psi | \\hat{H} | \\psi \\rangle\n"
"& = \\bigg(\\sum_{\\lambda'}a^*_{\\lambda'} \\langle \\lambda'|\\bigg) \\hat{H}\n"
"  \\bigg(\\sum_{\\lambda} a_\\lambda | \\lambda\\rangle\\bigg)\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\psi | \\hat{H} | \\psi \\rangle\n"
"& = \\bigg(\\sum_{\\lambda'}a^*_{\\lambda'} \\langle \\lambda'|\\bigg) \\hat{H}\n"
"  \\bigg(\\sum_{\\lambda} a_\\lambda | \\lambda\\rangle\\bigg)\\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& = \\sum_{\\lambda}\\sum_{\\lambda'} a^*_{\\lambda'}a_{\\lambda}\n"
"  \\langle \\lambda'|\\hat{H}| \\lambda\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"& = \\sum_{\\lambda}\\sum_{\\lambda'} a^*_{\\lambda'}a_{\\lambda}\n"
"  \\langle \\lambda'|\\hat{H}| \\lambda\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& = \\sum_{\\lambda}\\sum_{\\lambda'} a^*_{\\lambda'}a_{\\lambda} \\lambda\n"
"\\langle \\lambda'| \\lambda\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"& = \\sum_{\\lambda}\\sum_{\\lambda'} a^*_{\\lambda'}a_{\\lambda} \\lambda\n"
"\\langle \\lambda'| \\lambda\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& = \\sum_{\\lambda}\\sum_{\\lambda'} a^*_{\\lambda'}a_{\\lambda} \\lambda\n"
"\\cdot \\delta_{\\lambda, \\lambda'}\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"& = \\sum_{\\lambda}\\sum_{\\lambda'} a^*_{\\lambda'}a_{\\lambda} \\lambda\n"
"\\cdot \\delta_{\\lambda, \\lambda'}\\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\sum_\\lambda |a_\\lambda|^2 \\lambda\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\sum_\\lambda |a_\\lambda|^2 \\lambda\\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\sum_\\lambda p_\\lambda \\lambda\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\sum_\\lambda p_\\lambda \\lambda\\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"Since we do not know the eigenvalues or eigenstates of the target observable $\\hat{H}$, first we need to consider its diagonalization. Given that $\\hat{H}$ is <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A Hermitian is a square matrix that is equal to its own conjugate transpose, or a linear operator that is self-adjoint.\">Hermitian</DefinitionTooltip>, there exists a unitary transformation $V$ such that $\\hat{H}=V^\\dagger \\Lambda V$, where $\\Lambda$ is the diagonal eigenvalue matrix, so $\\langle j | \\Lambda | k \\rangle = 0$ if $j\\neq k$, and $\\langle j | \\Lambda | j \\rangle = \\lambda_j$.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"Since we do not know the eigenvalues or eigenstates of the target observable $\\hat{H}$, first we need to consider its diagonalization. Given that $\\hat{H}$ is <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A Hermitian is a square matrix that is equal to its own conjugate transpose, or a linear operator that is self-adjoint.\">Hermitian</DefinitionTooltip>, there exists a unitary transformation $V$ such that $\\hat{H}=V^\\dagger \\Lambda V$, where $\\Lambda$ is the diagonal eigenvalue matrix, so $\\langle j | \\Lambda | k \\rangle = 0$ if $j\\neq k$, and $\\langle j | \\Lambda | j \\rangle = \\lambda_j$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This implies that the expected value can be rewritten as:\n"
msgstr "Isso implica que o valor esperado pode ser reescrito como:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\hat{H}|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"& = \\langle\\psi|V^\\dagger \\Lambda V|\\psi\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\hat{H}|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"& = \\langle\\psi|V^\\dagger \\Lambda V|\\psi\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& = \\langle\\psi|V^\\dagger \\bigg(\\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1} |j\\rangle\n"
"\\langle j|\\bigg) \\Lambda \\bigg(\\sum_{k=0}^{2^n-1} |k\\rangle \\langle k|\\bigg) V|\\psi\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"& = \\langle\\psi|V^\\dagger \\bigg(\\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1} |j\\rangle\n"
"\\langle j|\\bigg) \\Lambda \\bigg(\\sum_{k=0}^{2^n-1} |k\\rangle \\langle k|\\bigg) V|\\psi\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& = \\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1} \\sum_{k=0}^{2^n-1}\\langle\\psi|V^\\dagger |j\\rangle\n"
"\\langle j| \\Lambda  |k\\rangle \\langle k| V|\\psi\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"& = \\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1} \\sum_{k=0}^{2^n-1}\\langle\\psi|V^\\dagger |j\\rangle\n"
"\\langle j| \\Lambda  |k\\rangle \\langle k| V|\\psi\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& = \\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1}\\langle\\psi|V^\\dagger |j\\rangle\n"
"\\langle j| \\Lambda  |j\\rangle \\langle j| V|\\psi\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"& = \\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1}\\langle\\psi|V^\\dagger |j\\rangle\n"
"\\langle j| \\Lambda  |j\\rangle \\langle j| V|\\psi\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1}|\\langle j| V|\\psi\\rangle|^2 \\lambda_j\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1}|\\langle j| V|\\psi\\rangle|^2 \\lambda_j\\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Given that if a system is in the state $|\\phi\\rangle = V |\\psi\\rangle$ the probability of measuring $| j\\rangle$ is $p_j = |\\langle j|\\phi \\rangle|^2$, the above expected value can be expressed as:\n"
msgstr "Dado que, se um sistema está no estado $|\\phi\\rangle = V |\\psi\\rangle$, a probabilidade de medir $| j\\rangle$ é $p_j = |\\langle j|\\phi \\rangle|^2$, o valor esperado acima pode ser expresso como:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\hat{H}|\\psi\\rangle =\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1} p_j \\lambda_j.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\hat{H}|\\psi\\rangle =\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1} p_j \\lambda_j.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is very important to note that the probabilities are taken from the state $V |\\psi\\rangle$ instead of $|\\psi\\rangle$. This is why the matrix $V$ is absolutely necessary.\n"
"You might be wondering how to obtain the matrix $V$ and the eigenvalues $\\Lambda$. If you already had the eigenvalues, then there would be no need to use a quantum computer since the goal of variational algorithms is to find these eigenvalues of $\\hat{H}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"É muito importante observar que as probabilidades são obtidas do estado $V |\\psi\\rangle$ e não de $|\\psi\\rangle$. É por isso que a matriz $V$ é absolutamente necessária.\n"
"Você pode estar se perguntando como obter a matriz $V$ e os autovalores $\\Lambda$. Se você já tivesse os autovalores, não haveria necessidade de usar um computador quântico, uma vez que o objetivo dos algoritmos variacionais é justamente encontrar esses autovalores de $\\hat{H}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Fortunately, there is a way around that: any $2^n \\times 2^n$ matrix can be written as a linear combination of $4^n$ tensor products of $n$ Pauli matrices and identities, all of which are both hermitian and unitary with known $V$ and $\\Lambda$. This is what Runtime's `Estimator` does internally by decomposing any [`Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) object into a [`SparsePauliOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp).\n"
msgid "Fortunately, there is a way around that: any $2^n \\times 2^n$ matrix can be written as a linear combination of $4^n$ tensor products of $n$ Pauli matrices and identities, all of which are both hermitian and unitary with known $V$ and $\\Lambda$. This is what the IBM Quantum `Estimator` does internally by decomposing any [`Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) object into a [`SparsePauliOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp).\n"
msgstr "Felizmente, existe uma alternativa: qualquer matriz $2^n \\times 2^n$ pode ser escrita como uma combinação linear de $4^n$ produtos tensoriais de $n$ matrizes de Pauli e identidades, todas hermitianas e unitárias com $V$ e $\\Lambda$ conhecidos. É isso que o `Estimator` do Runtime faz internamente, decompondo qualquer objeto [`Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) em um [`SparsePauliOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here are the Operators that can be used:\n"
msgstr "Aqui estão os Operadores que podem ser usados:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c}\n"
"  \\text{Operator} & \\sigma & V & \\Lambda \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  I & \\sigma_0 = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} & V_0 = I & \\Lambda_0 = I = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\\\[4mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c}\n"
"  \\text{Operator} & \\sigma & V & \\Lambda \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  I & \\sigma_0 = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} & V_0 = I & \\Lambda_0 = I = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\\\[4mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  X & \\sigma_1 = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix} & V_1 = H =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\end{pmatrix} & \\Lambda_1 = \\sigma_3 = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\end{pmatrix} \\\\[4mm]\n"
msgstr "  X & \\sigma_1 = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix} & V_1 = H =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\end{pmatrix} & \\Lambda_1 = \\sigma_3 = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\end{pmatrix} \\\\[4mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Y & \\sigma_2 = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & -i \\\\ i & 0 \\end{pmatrix} & V_2 = HS^\\dagger  =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\cdot  \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -i \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -i \\\\ 1 & i \\end{pmatrix}\\quad & \\Lambda_2 = \\sigma_3 = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\end{pmatrix} \\\\[4mm]\n"
msgstr "  Y & \\sigma_2 = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & -i \\\\ i & 0 \\end{pmatrix} & V_2 = HS^\\dagger  =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\cdot  \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -i \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -i \\\\ 1 & i \\end{pmatrix}\\quad & \\Lambda_2 = \\sigma_3 = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\end{pmatrix} \\\\[4mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Z & \\sigma_3 = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\end{pmatrix} & V_3 = I & \\Lambda_3 = \\sigma_3 = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
"So let's rewrite $\\hat{H}$ with respect to the Paulis and identities:\n"
msgstr ""
"  Z & \\sigma_3 = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\end{pmatrix} & V_3 = I & \\Lambda_3 = \\sigma_3 = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
"Então vamos reescrever $\\hat{H}$ em termos dos Paulis e identidades:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} =\n"
"\\sum_{k_{n-1}=0}^3...\n"
"\\sum_{k_0=0}^3 w_{k_{n-1}...k_0}\n"
"\\sigma_{k_{n-1}}\\otimes ... \\otimes \\sigma_{k_0} = \\sum_{k=0}^{4^n-1} w_k \\hat{P}_k,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} =\n"
"\\sum_{k_{n-1}=0}^3...\n"
"\\sum_{k_0=0}^3 w_{k_{n-1}...k_0}\n"
"\\sigma_{k_{n-1}}\\otimes ... \\otimes \\sigma_{k_0} = \\sum_{k=0}^{4^n-1} w_k \\hat{P}_k,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $k = \\sum_{l=0}^{n-1} 4^l k_l \\equiv k_{n-1}...k_0$ for $k_{n-1},...,k_0\\in \\{0,1,2,3\\}$ (that is, base $4$), and $\\hat{P}_{k} := \\sigma_{k_{n-1}}\\otimes ... \\otimes \\sigma_{k_0}$:\n"
msgstr "onde $k = \\sum_{l=0}^{n-1} 4^l k_l \\equiv k_{n-1}...k_0$ para $k_{n-1},...,k_0\\in \\{0,1,2,3\\}$ (ou seja, base $4$) e $\\hat{P}_{k} := \\sigma_{k_{n-1}}\\otimes ... \\otimes \\sigma_{k_0}$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\hat{H}|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"& = \\sum_{k=0}^{4^n-1} w_k\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1}|\\langle j| V_k|\\psi\\rangle|^2 \\langle j| \\Lambda_k |j\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\hat{H}|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"& = \\sum_{k=0}^{4^n-1} w_k\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1}|\\langle j| V_k|\\psi\\rangle|^2 \\langle j| \\Lambda_k |j\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\sum_{k=0}^{4^n-1} w_k \\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj}, \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\sum_{k=0}^{4^n-1} w_k \\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj}, \\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $V_k := V_{k_{n-1}}\\otimes ... \\otimes V_{k_0}$ and $\\Lambda_k := \\Lambda_{k_{n-1}}\\otimes ... \\otimes \\Lambda_{k_0}$, such that: $\\hat{P_k}=V_k^\\dagger \\Lambda_k V_k$.\n"
msgstr "onde $V_k := V_{k_{n-1}}\\otimes ... \\otimes V_{k_0}$ e $\\Lambda_k := \\Lambda_{k_{n-1}}\\otimes ... \\otimes \\Lambda_{k_0}$, de forma que: $\\hat{P_k}=V_k^\\dagger \\Lambda_k V_k.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cost functions {#cost-functions}"
msgstr "Funções de custo {#cost-functions}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In general, cost functions are used to describe the goal of a problem and how well a trial state is performing with respect to that goal. This definition can be applied to various examples in chemistry, machine learning, finance, optimization, and so on.\n"
msgstr "Em geral, funções de custo são usadas para descrever o objetivo de um problema e avaliar o quão bem um estado candidato está se saindo em relação a esse objetivo. Essa definição pode ser aplicada a diversos exemplos em química, aprendizado de máquina, finanças, otimização, entre outros.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's consider a simple example of finding the ground state of a system. Our objective is to minimize the expectation value of the observable representing energy (Hamiltonian $\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}$):\n"
msgstr "Vamos considerar um exemplo simples de encontrar o estado fundamental de um sistema. Nosso objetivo é minimizar o valor esperado do observável que representa a energia (Hamiltoniano $\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}$):\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{\\vec\\theta} \\langle\\psi(\\vec\\theta)|\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{\\vec\\theta} \\langle\\psi(\\vec\\theta)|\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can use the `Estimator` to evaluate the expectation value and pass this value to an optimizer to minimize. If the optimization is successful, it will return a set of optimal parameter values $\\vec\\theta^*$, from which we will be able to construct the proposed solution state $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta^*)\\rangle$ and compute the observed expectation value as $C(\\vec\\theta^*)$.\n"
msgstr "Podemos usar o `Estimator` para calcular o valor esperado e passar esse valor a um otimizador para minimizá-lo. Se a otimização for bem-sucedida, ela retornará um conjunto de valores ótimos de parâmetros $\\vec\\theta^*$, a partir dos quais poderemos construir o estado solução proposto $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta^*)\\rangle$ e calcular o valor esperado observado como $C(\\vec\\theta^*)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notice how we will only be able to minimize the cost function for the limited set of states that we are considering. This leads us to two separate possibilities:\n"
msgstr "Observe que só conseguiremos minimizar a função de custo para o conjunto limitado de estados que estamos considerando. Isso nos leva a duas possibilidades distintas:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Our ansatz does not define the solution state across the search space**: If this is the case, our optimizer will never find the solution, and we need to experiment with other ansatzes that might be able to represent our search space more accurately.\n"
msgstr "**Nosso ansatz não define o estado solução ao longo do espaço de busca**: Se for esse o caso, o otimizador nunca encontrará a solução, e precisamos experimentar outros ansatzes que possam representar nosso espaço de busca com mais precisão.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Our optimizer is unable to find this valid solution**: Optimization can be globally defined and locally defined. We'll explore what this means in the later section.\n"
msgstr "**Nosso otimizador não consegue encontrar essa solução válida**: A otimização pode ser definida de forma global ou local. Exploraremos o que isso significa na seção seguinte.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All in all, we will be performing a classical optimization loop but relying on the evaluation of the cost function to a quantum computer. From this perspective, one could think of the optimization as a purely classical endeavor where we call some <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A hypothetical device or software component that performs a specific function, but the internal workings of which are unknown. A user is only aware of the inputs and outputs of the black box, and has no knowledge of how the black box processes the inputs to produce the outputs.\">black-box quantum oracle</DefinitionTooltip> each time the optimizer needs to evaluate the cost function.\n"
msgstr "No geral, realizaremos um loop de otimização clássica, mas dependendo da avaliação da função de custo em um computador quântico. Nessa perspectiva, pode-se pensar na otimização como um processo puramente clássico em que chamamos um <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Um dispositivo hipotético ou componente de software que realiza uma função específica, mas cujo funcionamento interno é desconhecido. O usuário conhece apenas as entradas e saídas da caixa-preta, sem saber como ela processa as entradas para produzir as saídas.\">oráculo quântico de caixa-preta</DefinitionTooltip> cada vez que o otimizador precisa avaliar a função de custo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/extracted-outputs/a01a54f2-da16-4008-b422-fa7ded531f67-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Saída da célula de código anterior](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/extracted-outputs/a01a54f2-da16-4008-b422-fa7ded531f67-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will first carry this out using a simulator: the StatevectorEstimator. This is usually advisable for debugging, but we will immediately follow the debugging run with a calculation on real quantum hardware. Increasingly, problems of interest are no longer classically simulable without state-of-the-art supercomputing facilities.\n"
msgstr "Primeiro, executaremos isso usando um simulador: o StatevectorEstimator. Isso geralmente é recomendado para depuração, mas em seguida faremos o cálculo em hardware quântico real. Cada vez mais, os problemas de interesse deixam de ser classicamente simuláveis sem instalações de supercomputação de ponta.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "We will now proceed with running on a real quantum computer. Note the syntax changes. The steps involving the pass_manager will be discussed further in the next example. One step of particular importance in variational algorithms is the use of a Qiskit Runtime session. Starting a session allows you to run multiple iterations of a variational algorithm without waiting in a new queue each time parameters are updated. This is important if queue times are long and/or many iterations are needed. Only partners in the IBM Quantum&reg; Network can use Runtime sessions. If you do not have access to sessions, you can reduce the number of iterations you submit at a given time, and save the most recent parameters for use in future runs. If you submit too many iterations or encounter queue times that are too long, you may encounter error code 1217, which refers to long delays between job submissions.\n"
msgid "We will now proceed with running on a real quantum computer. Note the syntax changes. The steps involving the pass_manager will be discussed further in the next example. One step of particular importance in variational algorithms is the use of an IBM Quantum Compute Service session. Starting a session allows you to run multiple iterations of a variational algorithm without waiting in a new queue each time parameters are updated. This is important if queue times are long and/or many iterations are needed. Note that Open Plan users cannot use Quantum Compute sessions. If you do not have access to sessions, you can reduce the number of iterations you submit at a given time, and save the most recent parameters for use in future runs. If you submit too many iterations or encounter queue times that are too long, you may encounter error code 1217, which refers to long delays between job submissions.\n"
msgstr "Agora procederemos com a execução em um computador quântico real. Observe as mudanças de sintaxe. As etapas envolvendo o `pass_manager` serão discutidas com mais detalhes no próximo exemplo. Uma etapa de particular importância em algoritmos variacionais é o uso de uma sessão do Qiskit Runtime. Iniciar uma sessão permite executar várias iterações de um algoritmo variacional sem precisar aguardar em uma nova fila cada vez que os parâmetros são atualizados. Isso é importante quando os tempos de fila são longos e/ou muitas iterações são necessárias. Apenas parceiros da IBM Quantum&reg; Network podem usar sessões Runtime. Se você não tiver acesso a sessões, pode reduzir o número de iterações enviadas de uma vez e salvar os parâmetros mais recentes para uso em execuções futuras. Se você enviar iterações demais ou encontrar tempos de fila muito longos, poderá receber o código de erro 1217, que se refere a longos atrasos entre envios de jobs.\n"

