#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that in the present case, we will do this twice: once with optimization_level = 0, and once with it set to 3. Each time we will use the Estimator primitive to estimate the expectation values of the observable at different values of phase.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we can plot the results, and we see that the precision of the calculation was fairly good even without optimization, but it definitely improved by increasing optimization to level 3. Note that in deeper, more complicated circuits, the difference between optimization levels of 0 and 3 are likely to be more significant. This is a very simple circuit used as a toy model.\n"
msgstr "Por fim, podemos plotar os resultados e observar que a precisão do cálculo foi razoavelmente boa mesmo sem otimização, mas melhorou definitivamente ao aumentar a otimização para o nível 3. Observe que, em circuitos mais profundos e complexos, a diferença entre os níveis de otimização 0 e 3 tende a ser mais significativa. Este é um circuito muito simples usado como modelo de brinquedo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/extracted-outputs/f3d3f805-f8d0-474d-9a88-2d1f164639b0-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Saída da célula de código anterior](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/extracted-outputs/f3d3f805-f8d0-474d-9a88-2d1f164639b0-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Error Mitigation {#error-mitigation}"
msgstr "Mitigação de Erros {#error-mitigation}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Error mitigation](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques) refers to techniques that allow users to reduce circuit errors by modeling the device noise at the time of execution. Typically, this results in quantum pre-processing overhead related to model training and classical post-processing overhead to mitigate errors in the raw results by using the generated model.\n"
msgstr "A [mitigação de erros](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques) refere-se a técnicas que permitem aos usuários reduzir erros em circuitos modelando o ruído do dispositivo no momento da execução. Tipicamente, isso resulta em overhead de pré-processamento quântico relacionado ao treinamento do modelo e overhead de pós-processamento clássico para mitigar erros nos resultados brutos usando o modelo gerado.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "The Qiskit Runtime primitive's `resilience_level` option specifies the amount of resilience to build against errors. Higher levels generate more accurate results at the expense of longer processing times due to quantum sampling overhead. Resilience levels can be used to configure the trade-off between cost and accuracy when applying error mitigation to your primitive query.\n"
msgid "The IBM Quantum primitive's `resilience_level` option specifies the amount of resilience to build against errors. Higher levels generate more accurate results at the expense of longer processing times due to quantum sampling overhead. Resilience levels can be used to configure the trade-off between cost and accuracy when applying error mitigation to your primitive query.\n"
msgstr "A opção `resilience_level` das Primitivas do Qiskit Runtime especifica a quantidade de resiliência a ser construída contra erros. Níveis mais altos geram resultados mais precisos à custa de tempos de processamento mais longos, devido ao overhead de amostragem quântica. Os níveis de resiliência podem ser usados para configurar o equilíbrio entre custo e precisão ao aplicar mitigação de erros na sua consulta de Primitiva.\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When implementing any error mitigation technique, we expect the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A systematic drift in the measured quantities, usually caused by errors.\">bias</DefinitionTooltip> in our results to be reduced with respect to the previous, unmitigated bias. In some cases, the bias may even disappear. However, this comes at a cost. As we reduce the bias in our estimated quantities, the statistical variability will increase (that is, variance), which we can account for by further increasing the number of shots per circuit in our sampling process. This will introduce overhead beyond that needed to reduce the bias, so it is not done by default. We can easily opt-in to this behavior by adjusting the number of shots per circuit in options.executions.shots, as shown in the example below.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A diagram showing broader or narrowing distributions as in the bias/variance tradeoff.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/cost-function-bias-variance-trade-off.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Um diagrama mostrando distribuições mais largas ou mais estreitas, como no compromisso entre viés e variância.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/cost-function-bias-variance-trade-off.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "For this course, we will explore these error mitigation models at a high level to illustrate the error mitigation that Qiskit Runtime primitives can perform without requiring full implementation details.\n"
msgid "For this course, we will explore these error mitigation models at a high level to illustrate the error mitigation that IBM Quantum primitives can perform without requiring full implementation details.\n"
msgstr "Neste curso, exploraremos esses modelos de mitigação de erros em alto nível para ilustrar a mitigação que as Primitivas do Qiskit Runtime podem realizar, sem exigir detalhes completos de implementação.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirled readout error extinction (T-REx) {#twirled-readout-error-extinction-t-rex}"
msgstr "Extinção de erros de leitura com twirling (T-REx) {#twirled-readout-error-extinction-t-rex}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirled readout error extinction (T-REx) uses a technique known as Pauli twirling to reduce the noise introduced during the process of quantum measurement. This technique assumes no specific form of noise, which makes it very general and effective.\n"
msgstr "A extinção de erros de leitura com twirling (T-REx) usa uma técnica conhecida como Pauli twirling para reduzir o ruído introduzido durante o processo de medição quântica. Essa técnica não assume nenhuma forma específica de ruído, o que a torna bastante geral e eficaz.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overall workflow:\n"
msgstr "Fluxo de trabalho geral:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Acquire data for the zero state with randomized bit flips (Pauli X before measurement)\n"
msgstr "Adquirir dados para o estado zero com inversões de bits aleatórias (Pauli X antes da medição)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Acquire data for the desired (noisy) state with randomized bit flips (Pauli X before measurement)\n"
msgstr "Adquirir dados para o estado desejado (ruidoso) com inversões de bits aleatórias (Pauli X antes da medição)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compute the special function for each data set, and divide.\n"
msgstr "Calcular a função especial para cada conjunto de dados e dividir.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A diagram showing measurement and calibration circuits for T-REX.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/cost-function-trex-data-collection.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Um diagrama mostrando circuitos de medição e calibração para o T-REX.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/cost-function-trex-data-collection.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can set this with `options.resilience_level = 1`, demonstrated in the example below.\n"
msgstr "Podemos configurar isso com `options.resilience_level = 1`, demonstrado no exemplo abaixo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero noise extrapolation {#zero-noise-extrapolation}"
msgstr "Extrapolação para zero ruído {#zero-noise-extrapolation}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero noise extrapolation (ZNE) works by first amplifying the noise in the circuit that is preparing the desired quantum state, obtaining measurements for several different levels of noise, and using those measurements to infer the noiseless result.\n"
msgstr "A extrapolação para zero ruído (ZNE) funciona amplificando primeiro o ruído no circuito que está preparando o estado quântico desejado, obtendo medições para vários níveis diferentes de ruído e usando essas medições para inferir o resultado sem ruído.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Amplify circuit noise for several noise factors\n"
msgstr "Amplificar o ruído do circuito para vários fatores de ruído\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run every noise amplified circuit\n"
msgstr "Executar cada circuito com ruído amplificado\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extrapolate back to the zero noise limit\n"
msgstr "Extrapolar de volta para o limite de zero ruído\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A diagram showing steps in ZNE. Noise is artificially amplified by different factors. Then the values are extrapolated to what they should be at zero noise.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/cost-function-zne-stages.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Um diagrama mostrando as etapas do ZNE. O ruído é amplificado artificialmente por diferentes fatores. Em seguida, os valores são extrapolados para o que deveriam ser com zero ruído.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/cost-function-zne-stages.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can set this with `options.resilience_level = 2`. We can optimize this further by exploring a variety of `noise_factors`, `noise_amplifiers`, and `extrapolators`, but this is outside the scope of this course. We encourage you to experiment with these [options as described here](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques).\n"
msgstr "Podemos configurar isso com `options.resilience_level = 2`. Podemos otimizar ainda mais explorando uma variedade de `noise_factors`, `noise_amplifiers` e `extrapolators`, mas isso está fora do escopo deste curso. Encorajamos você a experimentar essas [opções conforme descritas aqui](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each method comes with its own associated overhead: a trade-off between the number of quantum computations needed (time) and the accuracy of our results:\n"
msgstr "Cada método vem com seu próprio overhead associado: um compromisso entre o número de computações quânticas necessárias (tempo) e a precisão dos nossos resultados:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c}\n"
"  \\text{Methods} & R=1 \\text{, T-REx} & R=2 \\text{, ZNE} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  \\text{Assumptions} & \\text{None} & \\text{Ability to scale noise} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\text{Qubit overhead} & 1 & 1 \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\text{Sampling overhead} & 2 & N_{\\text{noise-factors}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\text{Bias} & 0 & \\mathcal{O}(\\lambda^{N_{\\text{noise-factors}}}) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c}\n"
"  \\text{Methods} & R=1 \\text{, T-REx} & R=2 \\text{, ZNE} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  \\text{Assumptions} & \\text{None} & \\text{Ability to scale noise} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\text{Qubit overhead} & 1 & 1 \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\text{Sampling overhead} & 2 & N_{\\text{noise-factors}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\text{Bias} & 0 & \\mathcal{O}(\\lambda^{N_{\\text{noise-factors}}}) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

